00:02:45.552 --> 00:02:49.737
CS test takers identify as female. Now, this

00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:52.737
bar chart is helpful for answering certain types of questions.

00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:55.737
It's helpful for learning some information.

00:02:55.737 --> 00:02:58.737
But there are other ways that we can visualize this data as well.

00:02:58.737 --> 00:02:59.721
For example,

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:08.841
we can make a histogram. Let's look at the same value as before: Total Percent Female.

00:03:08.841 --> 00:03:16.706
When we make a histogram, the first thing we need to decide is the bucket size, or the range that each category is going to represent.

00:03:16.706 --> 00:03:19.691
In this case, percent. So we can have each category be

00:03:19.691 --> 00:03:27.571
2%, and this is what the chart would look like. We can have it be 10%, and this is

00:03:27.571 --> 00:03:29.675
